  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_015 (image_only, resnet50) scored 0.208 while config_008 (multimodal, pca_n2000+resnet50, concat) scored 0.527, indicating RNA is the dominant signal. However, we cannot yet decompose how much of the 0.527 comes from RNA alone versus synergistic interaction with image. Question: config_045 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) uses the exact same RNA encoder as our best model, giving a clean single-variable comparison. If RNA-only ≈ 0.527, image adds little and we can simplify; if RNA-only is substantially lower, the multimodal combination is genuinely synergistic and further multimodal optimization is warranted. Why this is the best next experiment: it is the single most informative missing data point for the modality-contribution question, uses the same encoder as the current best to isolate one variable, and directly informs whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion/aggregation refinements or in RNA-encoder improvements."
}

